From: "iLinux local research (AI-generated draft)" <local@invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] soc: apple: sart: Shift paddr and size by their own shift

sart_set_entry() checks the alignment of paddr against paddr_shift and of
size against size_shift, but then shifts paddr by size_shift and size by
paddr_shift.  Every SART version supported so far uses 12 for both, so
this has no functional effect today; fix it before a version with
different shifts is added.

Found by reading the code while adding SARTv4; untested.

NOT FOR UPSTREAM SUBMISSION: AI-generated local research draft (Asahi
Linux generative-AI policy).  No Signed-off-by on purpose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sart.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sart.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sart.c
index 9eaf3feb..4a3b4965 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sart.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sart.c
@@ -253,8 +253,8 @@ static int sart_set_entry(struct apple_sart *sart, int index, u8 flags,
 	if (paddr & ((1 << sart->ops->paddr_shift) - 1))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	paddr >>= sart->ops->size_shift;
-	size >>= sart->ops->paddr_shift;
+	paddr >>= sart->ops->paddr_shift;
+	size >>= sart->ops->size_shift;
 
 	if (size > sart->ops->size_max)
 		return -EINVAL;
